course: dictionary
lesson: 3339
title: Words that change over time
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Evolve is a verb, and its forms are evolve, evolves, evolved and evolving. Its first meaning is for living things: it means to change slowly, over a very long time and many generations, as animals and plants adapt to where they live. «Whales evolved from land animals» tells you the change took a very long time.
explain: Evolve can also mean to develop or change gradually into something better or more complex. «The plan evolved over time» does not mean the plan changed in one second. It changed bit by bit as people worked on it.
explain: Use the context clues. Words like «over a very long time», «many generations» and «over time» all point to slow change. In some games, a character evolves into a stronger form very suddenly. That is a game meaning, not real evolution, so check the sentence before you decide what evolve means.
fact: Evolve means to change slowly, over many generations.
fact: «Polar bears evolved from brown bears within the last few hundred thousand years.»
fact: «Birds evolved from small feathered meat-eating dinosaurs called theropods.»
fact: Charles Darwin studied how living things change over time. He described natural selection: living things best suited to their environment survive and have more young.
fact: In games, evolve can mean a sudden change, which is different from real evolution.
exercise: «Polar bears evolved from brown bears within the last few hundred thousand years.» What does evolved mean here? | Painted their fur white | *Changed slowly over a very long time | Fell asleep in the snow | Ran away quickly
exercise: In a game, your character evolves into a stronger form. Is this real evolution, like whales? | No, because the character has no legs | *No, games use the word loosely for a sudden change | Yes, because all characters are living things | Yes, it takes millions of years
exercise: «The plan evolved over time.» Which word could replace evolved? | froze | vanished | *developed gradually | shouted
test: «Mexican tetra fish trapped in dark caves evolved to lose their eyes and colour, because eyes are useless in darkness.» What does evolved mean here? | *Changed slowly over many generations to suit the caves | Painted themselves bright | Moved to a new cave in one day | Grew bigger eyes
test: Ben says the new phone app evolved in one night. Which word in the sentence shows that evolve can mean develop gradually? | *It does not show it: a change in one night is quick, not gradual | Phone | Night | Ben
exam: «Birds evolved from small feathered dinosaurs.» Explain in your own words what evolved means, using the words over a very long time. | Flew away from the dinosaurs at once | Stopped being dinosaurs for a day | Were made in a factory | *Changed slowly over a very long time into a new kind of animal
